    <h2>What Is NordVPN?</h2>
    <p>NordVPN is a VPN service launched in 2012 by four childhood friends in Lithuania. The company is now headquartered in Panama, which has no mandatory data retention laws, making it a privacy-friendly jurisdiction. NordVPN has grown into one of the most recognized VPN brands in the world, serving over 14 million users across 111 countries. The service is known for its speed, security features, and aggressive marketing campaigns featuring celebrities and sports sponsorships.</p>
    <p>The current pricing starts at $3.09 per month on a 24-month plan, which includes access to over 6,400 servers in 111 countries. NordVPN uses its proprietary NordLynx protocol, built around WireGuard, to deliver some of the fastest VPN speeds measured in independent tests. The service also offers Double VPN for routing traffic through two servers, Onion Over VPN for Tor integration, and a Threat Protection feature that blocks ads, trackers, and malicious domains. NordVPN has been independently audited twice, once by PwC in 2018 and again by Deloitte in 2022, confirming its no-logs policy.</p>

    <h2>What Is Surfshark?</h2>
    <p>Surfshark is a VPN service launched in 2018 and headquartered in the Netherlands. Despite being a younger company than NordVPN, Surfshark has rapidly grown into a top-tier VPN known for aggressive pricing and unlimited device connections. The service serves users across 100 countries and has built a reputation for offering premium features at a budget price point. Surfshark is registered in the Netherlands, which is subject to EU GDPR regulations but has no mandatory data retention laws for VPNs.</p>
    <p>The current pricing starts at $2.19 per month on a 24-month plan, which includes access to over 3,200 servers in 100 countries. Surfshark uses WireGuard as its primary protocol and offers MultiHop for double VPN connections, CleanWeb for ad and tracker blocking, and Camouflage Mode for obfuscation. Surfshark was independently audited by Deloitte in 2021, confirming its no-logs policy. The defining feature is unlimited simultaneous connections on a single subscription, which makes it the best value VPN for families and users with many devices.</p>

    <h2>Speed and Performance</h2>
    <p>Speed is the most measurable difference between NordVPN and Surfshark. Both use WireGuard-based protocols, but NordVPN's NordLynx implementation consistently outperforms Surfshark in independent benchmarks.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Speed Results</h3>
    <p>In 2026 speed tests on a 500 Mbps baseline connection, NordVPN using NordLynx retained over 90% of baseline speed on nearby servers (under 500 miles) and over 70% on distant servers (over 3,000 miles). Latency increased by only 5 to 15 milliseconds on nearby servers, which is barely noticeable for browsing or video calls. For 4K streaming, NordVPN can sustain the 25 Mbps required without buffering on most servers.</p>
    <p>NordVPN also offers dedicated P2P servers optimized for file sharing. These servers deliver consistent speeds of 200+ Mbps on a fast baseline connection, which makes NordVPN one of the fastest VPNs for torrenting.</p>

    <h3>Surfshark Speed Results</h3>
    <p>Surfshark using WireGuard retained around 80% of baseline speed on nearby servers and 60% on distant servers in the same tests. Latency increased by 10 to 25 milliseconds on nearby servers, which is still acceptable for browsing but noticeable in competitive gaming. For 4K streaming, Surfshark can sustain the required bandwidth on most servers but may buffer occasionally on distant or congested servers.</p>
    <p>Surfshark does not offer dedicated P2P servers, but its general servers handle torrenting well enough for most users. Speeds typically range from 100 to 200 Mbps on a fast connection, which is sufficient for downloading large files.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best overall speed goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Surfshark is fast enough for most users but cannot match NordVPN's consistency on distant servers.</p>

    <h2>Server Network and Coverage</h2>
    <p>The size and distribution of a VPN's server network affects speed, streaming access, and the ability to bypass geo-restrictions. NordVPN has roughly twice as many servers as Surfshark, but Surfshark covers nearly as many countries.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Server Network</h3>
    <p>NordVPN operates over 6,400 physical servers across 111 countries. This is one of the largest server networks among consumer VPNs. More servers means less congestion and better odds of finding a fast server near you. NordVPN also offers specialty servers including Double VPN, Onion Over VPN, and P2P-optimized servers. All servers run on RAM-only infrastructure, meaning data is wiped on every reboot.</p>

    <h3>Surfshark Server Network</h3>
    <p>Surfshark operates over 3,200 servers across 100 countries. While smaller than NordVPN's network, this is still sufficient coverage for most users. Surfshark's servers are also RAM-only and the company has been expanding aggressively. Surfshark offers MultiHop for double VPN connections and NoBorders mode for bypassing restrictive networks in countries like China and Iran.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best server coverage goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Surfshark covers enough countries for most users but has fewer servers per location, which can mean congestion during peak hours.</p>

    <h2>Streaming Performance</h2>
    <p>Both NordVPN and Surfshark are excellent for unblocking streaming platforms, but NordVPN has a slight edge due to more server locations and dedicated streaming-optimized servers.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Streaming</h3>
    <p>NordVPN unblocks Netflix libraries in over 15 countries including US, UK, Japan, Canada, and Australia. It also reliably unblocks Disney Plus, BBC iPlayer, Hulu, HBO Max, Amazon Prime Video, and YouTube Premium. NordVPN does not advertise specific streaming servers, but its SmartPlay technology automatically routes you to a server that can unblock the platform you are trying to watch. In 2026 tests, NordVPN unblocked every major streaming platform on the first try.</p>

    <h3>Surfshark Streaming</h3>
    <p>Surfshark unblocks Netflix in over 15 countries and reliably accesses Disney Plus, BBC iPlayer, Hulu, HBO Max, and Amazon Prime Video. Surfshark's NoBorders mode helps bypass restrictions in countries with heavy censorship. In 2026 tests, Surfshark unblocked all major platforms but occasionally struggled with smaller regional Netflix libraries like Japan and South Korea on the first try, requiring a server switch.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best for streaming reliability goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Surfshark is a strong performer but NordVPN's larger server network gives it a slight edge for accessing niche libraries.</p>

    <h2>Privacy and Security</h2>
    <p>Both VPNs take privacy seriously with no-logs policies, RAM-only servers, and independent audits. The differences are in jurisdiction and advanced security features.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Privacy Features</h3>
    <p>NordVPN is headquartered in Panama, which has no mandatory data retention laws and is outside the Five Eyes and Fourteen Eyes surveillance alliances. The no-logs policy has been audited twice, by PwC in 2018 and Deloitte in 2022. NordVPN also publishes an annual transparency report detailing requests for user data and how the company responded. All servers are RAM-only, meaning data is wiped on every reboot. Advanced security features include Double VPN, Onion Over VPN, and a Threat Protection suite that blocks ads, trackers, and malware.</p>

    <h3>Surfshark Privacy Features</h3>
    <p>Surfshark is headquartered in the Netherlands, which is subject to EU GDPR but has no mandatory data retention laws for VPNs. The Netherlands is technically part of the Nine Eyes alliance, which concerns some privacy purists, but Surfshark's no-logs policy means there is nothing to share even if requested. The policy was audited by Deloitte in 2021. All servers are RAM-only. Advanced features include MultiHop for double VPN, CleanWeb for ad blocking, and Camouflage Mode for obfuscation.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best jurisdiction and audit history goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Surfshark is privacy-solid but its Netherlands jurisdiction is a minor concern for the most privacy-obsessed users.</p>

    <h2>Pricing and Value</h2>
    <p>Pricing is where Surfshark has a clear advantage. Surfshark is significantly cheaper than NordVPN and includes unlimited device connections on a single subscription.</p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Plan</th><th>NordVPN</th><th>Surfshark</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Monthly</td><td>$12.99/mo</td><td>$12.95/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>1-Year</td><td>$4.99/mo</td><td>$3.99/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2-Year</td><td>$3.09/mo</td><td>$2.19/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Simultaneous Connections</td><td>6</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Free Trial</td><td>7 days (mobile)</td><td>7 days (mobile)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Money-Back Guarantee</td><td>30 days</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Bundles Available</td><td>NordPass, NordLocker</td><td>Surfshark Antivirus, Surfshark Search</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>On a 24-month plan, Surfshark costs $2.19 per month versus NordVPN's $3.09. That is a 29% difference. When you factor in unlimited device connections, Surfshark is the clear value winner for families or users with more than 6 devices. NordVPN justifies the higher price with faster speeds, more servers, and a more polished app experience.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best price and value goes to <span class="winner-tag">Surfshark</span>. NordVPN is worth the premium if speed and server coverage matter more than price.</p>

    <h2>Apps and Ease of Use</h2>
    <p>Both VPNs offer apps for all major platforms, but NordVPN's apps are more polished and intuitive. Surfshark's apps are functional but slightly less refined.</p>

    <h3>NordVPN Apps</h3>
    <p>NordVPN offers native apps for Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, Android, Android TV, Apple TV, and routers. The apps feature a map-based interface that makes server selection intuitive. The Quick Connect button automatically picks the fastest server for your location. NordVPN also offers browser extensions for Chrome and Firefox that encrypt browser traffic only, which is faster than full-device VPN for users who only need to protect browsing.</p>

    <h3>Surfshark Apps</h3>
    <p>Surfshark offers native apps for Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, Android, Android TV, Apple TV, Fire TV, and routers. The apps use a list-based interface with search and favorites. Surfshark's Quick Connect is reliable and the app includes a pause feature that temporarily disconnects the VPN for 5 minutes, which is useful for accessing local-only services. Surfshark also offers browser extensions for Chrome and Firefox.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best app experience goes to <span class="winner-tag">NordVPN</span>. Surfshark's apps are solid but NordVPN's map interface and overall polish are superior.</p>

    <h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

    <h3>NordVPN Pros</h3>
    <div class="pros-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Fastest VPN speeds in independent tests</li>
        <li>6,400+ servers across 111 countries</li>
        <li>Headquartered in Panama, privacy-friendly</li>
        <li>Audited no-logs policy by PwC and Deloitte</li>
        <li>RAM-only servers with automatic data wipe</li>
        <li>Double VPN, Onion Over VPN, Threat Protection</li>
        <li>Polished apps with map-based server selection</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

