    <h2>Who Should Use Which?</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Streamers and Cord-Cutters</h3>
      <p>If your primary use is unblocking Netflix, Disney Plus, or BBC iPlayer, NordVPN is the better choice. Its larger server network and SmartPlay technology give you more reliable access to regional libraries, and the faster speeds mean less buffering in 4K. Surfshark works for streaming but occasionally requires server switching for smaller libraries.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Families and Multi-Device Users</h3>
      <p>If you have a household with more than 6 devices, Surfshark is the clear winner. Unlimited simultaneous connections means you can protect phones, tablets, laptops, smart TVs, and gaming consoles on a single subscription. NordVPN limits you to 6 devices, which is enough for an individual but not for a family.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Privacy Enthusiasts</h3>
      <p>If privacy is your top priority, NordVPN is the safer choice. Its Panama jurisdiction is outside all major surveillance alliances, and the no-logs policy has been audited twice. Surfshark is privacy-solid but its Netherlands jurisdiction is a minor concern for the most paranoid users, despite the audited no-logs policy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Budget-Conscious Users</h3>
      <p>If price is your primary concern, Surfshark offers the best value in the VPN market. At $2.19 per month on a 24-month plan with unlimited devices, it undercuts NordVPN by 29% while delivering 90% of the performance. For everyday browsing and occasional streaming, Surfshark is more than sufficient.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Remote Workers and Gamers</h3>
      <p>If you need a VPN for remote work or gaming, NordVPN's faster speeds and lower latency make it the better choice. Video calls, file transfers, and competitive gaming all benefit from NordVPN's consistent performance on nearby servers. Surfshark works for these use cases but the higher latency is noticeable in fast-paced games.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Real-World Use Cases</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
