    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is NordVPN better than Surfshark?</h3>
    <p>NordVPN is better for users who want the fastest speeds, the most polished apps, and advanced features like Double VPN and Onion Over VPN. Surfshark is better for budget-conscious users and large households because it allows unlimited simultaneous connections on a single subscription. For most users, NordVPN delivers a slightly better overall experience, but Surfshark offers better value if you need to connect many devices.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, NordVPN or Surfshark?</h3>
    <p>Surfshark is cheaper. Surfshark One costs around $2.19 per month on a 24-month plan, while NordVPN costs around $3.09 per month on the same term. Surfshark also includes unlimited device connections, while NordVPN limits you to 6 devices. If price is your primary concern and you have many devices, Surfshark is the better value. NordVPN justifies the higher price with faster speeds and more server locations.</p>

    <h3>Which VPN is better for streaming, NordVPN or Surfshark?</h3>
    <p>Both VPNs unblock Netflix, Disney Plus, BBC iPlayer, and most major streaming platforms. NordVPN has a slight edge because it maintains more server locations and has dedicated streaming-optimized servers. Surfshark matches NordVPN on most platforms but occasionally struggles with smaller regional libraries. For streaming Netflix US, UK, and Japan, both perform well. For less common libraries, NordVPN is more reliable.</p>

    <h3>Does NordVPN or Surfshark have more servers?</h3>
    <p>NordVPN has more servers at over 6,400 servers across 111 countries. Surfshark has over 3,200 servers across 100 countries. NordVPN offers more locations, which means better odds of finding a fast server near you. Surfshark's smaller network is still sufficient for most users and the company is actively expanding. If server diversity matters for accessing specific regions, NordVPN has the edge.</p>

    <h3>Which VPN is faster, NordVPN or Surfshark?</h3>
    <p>NordVPN is faster in independent speed tests. Using the NordLynx protocol, NordVPN retains over 90% of baseline internet speed on nearby servers and over 70% on distant servers. Surfshark using WireGuard retains around 80% on nearby servers and 60% on distant servers. For 4K streaming, large downloads, or gaming, NordVPN delivers a more consistent experience. For everyday browsing, the speed difference is barely noticeable.</p>

    <h3>Can I use NordVPN and Surfshark together?</h3>
    <p>You can install both VPNs on the same device, but you cannot run them simultaneously because they conflict at the network layer. Most users pick one and stick with it. A practical approach is to use NordVPN on your primary devices for speed and streaming, and Surfshark on secondary devices or for sharing with family members. Running both subscriptions is rarely worth the extra cost unless you have specific needs.</p>

